			io_k8s_api_core_v1_EndpointSubset {doc 'EndpointSubset is a group of addresses with a common set of ports The expanded set of endpoints is the Cartesian product of Addresses x Ports For example, given:		  Addresses: [ip: 101011, ip: 101022],	  Ports:     [name: a, port: 8675, name: b, port: 309]	The resulting set of endpoints can be viewed as:	a: [ 101011:8675, 101022:8675 ],	b: [ 101011:309, 101022:309 ]Deprecated: This API is deprecated in v133+'}
