								optional
									io_k8s_api_scheduling_v1beta1_PodGroupList_items_status_conditions cardinality [1..*] {doc 'conditions represent the latest observations of the PodGroup_s stateKnown condition types: - PodGroupInitiallyScheduled: Indicates whether the scheduling requirement has been satisfied Once this condition transitions to True, it serves as a terminal state and will never revert to False, even if pods are subsequently evicted and group constraints are no longer met - DisruptionTarget: Indicates whether the PodGroup is about to be terminated  due to disruption such as preemptionKnown reasons for the PodGroupInitiallyScheduled condition: - Unschedulable: The PodGroup cannot be scheduled due to resource constraints,  affinity/anti-affinity rules, or insufficient capacity for the gang- SchedulerError: The PodGroup cannot be scheduled due to some internal error  that happened during scheduling, for example due to nodeAffinity parsing errorsKnown reasons for the DisruptionTarget condition: - PreemptionByScheduler: The PodGroup was preempted by the scheduler to make room for  higher-priority PodGroups or Pods'}
